.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_REPLACE_PATH 3 2026-09-28 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_replace_path \- stage a named replacement from a filesystem path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_replace_path("
.BI "        mpq_patch_s *" "patch,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        const char *" "source_path,"
.BI "        const mpq_file_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the complete file at \fIsource_path\fP and stages it as a replacement
for an existing named base member. It does not modify the base archive or
publish the patch. NULL \fIoptions\fP selects patch-writer defaults. Explicit
options control storage of the patch member, not the final patched file;
locale and platform must match the base member.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A missing member or invalid pointer returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST.
Locale/platform mismatches or unsupported options return LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT.
Opening, size, allocation, read, and close errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_begin_mpqe (3),
